<title>USA: EmCare settles with Justice Dept suit.</title>
<headline>EmCare settles with Justice Dept suit.</headline>
<text>
<p>DALLAS, Feb 12 (Reuter) EmCare Holdings Inc said Wednesday it has reached an agreement in principle with the U.S. Department of Justice to settle a suit alleging the improper coding of charges for emergency department services reimbursed under Medicare, Medicaid and other medical programs.</p>
<p>Under the agreement the firm will pay $7,750,000 to the United States and the various states, plus an additional $250,000 in legal fees.</p>
